**New evidence**
- UNICEF’s 2022 child-poverty package is a useful baseline for vulnerability and inequality, because it aggregates 2016-2022 PNAD data across income, education, information, water, sanitation, housing, and food.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pobreza Multidimensional na Infância e Adolescência no Brasil","publisher":"UNICEF Brasil","publication_date":"2023-02-14","url":"https://www.unicef.org/brazil/relatorios/as-multiplas-dimensoes-da-pobreza-na-infancia-e-na-adolescencia-no-brasil","claim":"The UNICEF study says more than 60% of Brazilians up to age 17 live in poverty, and that poverty is multidimensional, covering education, sanitation, water, food, housing, and information; it also says racial and regional inequalities remain severe.","locator":"Highlights section","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"UNICEF is a strong child-welfare monitor and the page explicitly summarizes the study's Brazil-wide findings from IBGE data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The study uses data extending through 2022 for some dimensions and is directly relevant to the Bolsonaro-to-Lula transition context.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly contextual rather than uniquely attributable to Bolsonaro; it reflects inherited structural conditions and pandemic-era deterioration during his term.","contrary_evidence":["This is a synthesis page, not a ruler-specific audit.","It does not isolate Bolsonaro from pandemic and subnational effects."],"lenses":["6B.3","6B.8","6B.10"]}

- UNICEF’s 2022 education note is a direct 2022 warning about exclusion from school.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Dois milhões de crianças e adolescentes de 11 a 19 anos não estão frequentando a escola no Brasil, alerta UNICEF","publisher":"UNICEF Brasil","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://www.unicef.org/brazil/innocenti/brazil/comunicados-de-imprensa/dois-milhoes-de-criancas-e-adolescentes-de-11-a-19-anos-nao-estao-frequentando-a-escola-no-brasil","claim":"UNICEF said 2 million children and adolescents aged 11 to 19 were not attending school in Brazil, equal to 11% of the survey sample, and linked the problem to child labor and learning difficulties.","locator":"Press-release body / lead paragraph","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"UNICEF is a credible independent source and the page reports a concrete 2022 survey result with a direct percentage.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Contextual, but relevant to Bolsonaro-era human-development outcomes and the government's responsibility to respond.","contrary_evidence":["The study identifies pandemic-era learning disruption and labor as major drivers, so attribution is partial.","It does not by itself show a specific Bolsonaro policy failure."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.10"]}

- The World Bank’s Brazil food-security note ties 2022 welfare conditions to food inflation and transfer policy.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Inflação de alimentos e insegurança alimentar no Brasil","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04-01","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/pt/country/brazil/publication/brazil-food-insecurity-and-food-inflation","claim":"The World Bank estimated that 30.7% of Brazil's population experienced moderate or severe food insecurity in 2022, and projected poverty at about 24.3% for 2022 as labor-market recovery and Bolsa Família adjustments offset some losses.","locator":"Body text on food insecurity, poverty, and labor-market recovery","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank analysis is high-quality and directly quantifies 2022 household hardship and the role of cash transfers.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Explicitly discusses 2022 conditions, with some projections made during the year and retrospective comparisons to 2019-2021.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly contextual, but relevant because social-protection design and inflation response during Bolsonaro's administration affected household exposure.","contrary_evidence":["The note also says labor-market recovery helped and that transfer programs cushioned losses.","It does not isolate Bolsonaro from inherited pandemic effects or global food shocks."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.6","6B.8","6B.10"]}

- Bolsonaro-era Auxílio Brasil expansion shows direct cash support to vulnerable families.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Quase 500 mil famílias passam a integrar o programa Auxílio Brasil em outubro","publisher":"Government of Brazil","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.gov.br/pt-br/noticias/assistencia-social/2022/10/quase-500-mil-familias-passam-a-integrar-o-programa-auxilio-brasil-em-outubro","claim":"The government said about 500,000 poor or extremely poor families were added to Auxílio Brasil in October 2022, bringing coverage to 21.1 million families and guaranteeing a minimum payment of R$600 per family.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official program announcement with a clear beneficiary count and benefit floor.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Bolsonaro administration's cash-transfer policy and election-year execution, though some components were congressional or constitutional in origin.","contrary_evidence":["The announcement is a policy claim, not an independent outcome evaluation.","The expansion also had an obvious election-year political dimension."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.7","6B.10"]}

- The Auxílio Brasil framework shows health and education conditionalities plus social oversight.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"D10852","publisher":"Planalto","publication_date":"2022-11-08","url":"https://planalto.gov.br/ccivil_03/_ato2019-2022/2021/decreto/d10852.htm","claim":"The decree assigns health and education ministries responsibility for tracking Auxílio Brasil conditionalities, requires information sharing with the Ministry of Citizenship, and provides for social-assistance priority and review when families miss conditions.","locator":"Arts. 43-47 in the decree text","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary legal text with explicit operational rules for a national cash-transfer program.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The decree text was in force during 2022 and directly governed that year’s program.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential system design under Bolsonaro, though implementation depended on ministries and subnational networks.","contrary_evidence":["Conditionalities do not prove high-quality delivery.","The text can exist even if enforcement is uneven."],"lenses":["6B.4","6B.5","6B.7"]}

- The 2022 Portaria update shows active monitoring and a built-in correction mechanism.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Informe Auxílio Brasil 838","publisher":"Ministério da Cidadania / Governo do Brasil","publication_date":"2022-05-30","url":"https://www.mds.gov.br/webarquivos/sala_de_imprensa/boletins/boletim_auxilio_brasil/2022/maio/Boletim_PAB_Informa_838.html","claim":"The ministry said the first 2022 education-conditionality monitoring period was discarded because of technical and operational inconsistencies in the school-presence system, and the resulting sanction was annulled.","locator":"Communicado section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"This is the direct administrative notice explaining a corrective action taken for the program.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Bolsonaro-era welfare administration because it concerns program management and correction.","contrary_evidence":["It also shows that the program's monitoring system had implementation problems.","A correction does not prove overall service quality."],"lenses":["6B.5","6B.4","6B.7"]}

- The social-assistance ministry updated the targeting/focalization rules to improve payment accuracy.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Programa Auxílio Brasil atualiza os critérios de verificação de dados","publisher":"Casa Civil / Governo do Brasil","publication_date":"2022-09-05","url":"https://www.gov.br/casacivil/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/2022/setembro/programa-auxilio-brasil-atualiza-os-criterios-de-verificacao-de-dados","claim":"The government said Auxílio Brasil updated periodic data-verification rules to improve targeting by identifying discrepancies in family records against other federal databases.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official policy announcement describing a concrete administrative improvement to targeting and verification.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to the Bolsonaro administration's social-assistance management.","contrary_evidence":["Targeting upgrades do not guarantee better outcomes on the ground.","This is process evidence, not a household-impact evaluation."],"lenses":["6B.4","6B.5","6B.7"]}

- Bolsonaro’s government used federal funding to deliver school internet access for low-income pupils.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Governo Federal garante acesso à internet para alunos da rede pública","publisher":"Government of Brazil","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.gov.br/pt-br/noticias/educacao-e-pesquisa/2022/05/governo-federal-garante-acesso-a-internet-para-alunos-da-rede-publica/","claim":"Bolsonaro signed a law creating Internet Brasil, a program to provide free mobile broadband to public-school students from CadÚnico families.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official announcement of a signed law and the stated target population.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential action, although implementation was shared with the communications and education ministries.","contrary_evidence":["The page is promotional and does not measure take-up or learning gains.","Program creation is not the same as durable delivery."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.9"]}

- The legal decree for Internet Brasil shows a large targeted transfer for education connectivity.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"D10952","publisher":"Planalto","publication_date":"2022-02-09","url":"https://www.planalto.gov.br/CCivil_03/_Ato2019-2022/2022/Decreto/D10952.htm","claim":"The decree regulates the internet-access program for public-school students and teachers, authorizing a one-time transfer of R$3.501 billion to states and the Federal District for educational internet access and requiring transparent distribution criteria.","locator":"Art. 1 and paragraph 1","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary legal text with a specific budget amount and implementation conditions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's administration and its education-connectivity policy.","contrary_evidence":["The transfer is still a delivery mechanism, not an outcome measure.","Actual access gains depended on state and municipal execution."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.9"]}

- Anatel’s school-connectivity pilot gives implementation evidence beyond mere announcement.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Conselho Diretor aprova piloto para conectividade nas escolas","publisher":"Anatel","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://www.gov.br/anatel/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/conselho-diretor-aprova-piloto-para-conectividades-nas-escolas","claim":"Anatel approved a pilot to bring broadband internet to 177 public basic-education schools by March 2023 as part of a R$3.1 billion school-connectivity commitment.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official regulator announcement with a concrete implementation milestone, though the commitment sits partly outside direct executive control.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 implementation context, with delivery extending into early 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Partly attributable to Bolsonaro-era policy design, but implementation was shared with regulators and telecom operators.","contrary_evidence":["This is a pilot, not a full-system roll-out.","The funding came from telecom obligations, not only presidential spending choices."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.5","6B.9"]}

- Bolsonaro’s health ministry mounted a large child-vaccination campaign in 2022.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ministério da Saúde lança Campanha Nacional de Vacinação contra a Poliomielite e Multivacinação neste domingo (7)","publisher":"Ministério da Saúde","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://www.gov.br/saude/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/2022/agosto/ministerio-da-saude-lanca-campanha-nacional-de-vacinacao-contra-a-poliomielite-e-multivacinacao-neste-domingo-7","claim":"The health ministry launched a nationwide polio and multivaccination campaign aimed at vaccinating at least 95% of children aged 1 to under 5 against polio and updating vaccines for children and adolescents under 15.","locator":"Lead paragraphs and campaign description","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry announcement with specific coverage targets and service scale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Bolsonaro's government through the Ministry of Health, though campaign results are not shown on the page.","contrary_evidence":["The announcement does not prove actual 95% coverage.","Vaccination campaigns were also responding to post-pandemic catch-up needs."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.6","6B.9"]}

- The ministry also explicitly added COVID vaccination for small children at the end of 2022.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ministério da Saúde incorpora vacina Covid-19 para crianças de 6 meses a menores de 5 anos no SUS","publisher":"Ministério da Saúde","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.gov.br/saude/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/2022/dezembro/ministerio-da-saude-incorpora-vacina-covid-19-para-criancas-de-6-meses-a-menores-de-5-anos-no-sus/","claim":"The health ministry said Conitec favorably recommended incorporating Pfizer's COVID-19 vaccine for children aged 6 months to under 5 years into the SUS.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry notice reporting a formal incorporation recommendation for a vulnerable age group.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's health ministry decisions at the end of his term, though procurement and rollout were also constrained by technical processes.","contrary_evidence":["This is a recommendation/incorporation notice rather than verified uptake.","It comes at the very end of the period."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.6","6B.8"]}

- Indigenous health was treated as a priority area, with large numbers of attendances and targeted actions.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Assistência à população indígena foi uma das prioridades durante a pandemia de Covid-19; conheça as ações","publisher":"Ministério da Saúde","publication_date":"2022-12-20","url":"https://www.gov.br/saude/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/2022/dezembro/assistencia-a-populacao-indigena-foi-uma-das-prioridades-durante-a-pandemia-de-covid-19-conheca-as-acoes","claim":"The ministry said that from 2019 to November 2022 it delivered more than 53 million primary-care attendances to indigenous peoples and that 20 health actions were carried out from 2020 to 2022 inside indigenous territories.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry report with specific service counts and a defined target population.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly spans the Bolsonaro period through late 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Bolsonaro's federal health administration, though the delivery depends heavily on specialized indigenous-health structures.","contrary_evidence":["Official summaries can overstate effective quality or continuity of care.","The page does not independently verify health outcomes."],"lenses":["6B.3","6B.6","6B.9"]}

- Bolsonaro’s housing program expanded support for low-income households, including bigger subsidies.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Governo Federal amplia os limites do apoio financeiro do programa de habitação popular Casa Verde e Amarela","publisher":"Government of Brazil","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://www.gov.br/pt-br/noticias/assistencia-social/2022/03/governo-federal-amplia-os-limites-do-apoio-financeiro-do-programa-de-habitacao-popular-casa-verde-e-amarela","claim":"The government expanded Casa Verde e Amarela financial support so urban households could receive up to R$130,000 and rural households up to R$55,000 for purchase, construction, or renovation.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official announcement of a concrete change in housing support limits under a presidential decree.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential action under Bolsonaro, though impacts on housing affordability depend on credit access and execution.","contrary_evidence":["This is a financing ceiling, not a delivery result.","Housing support can still be unevenly distributed."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.9","6B.10"]}

- The 2022 census release gives hard evidence of water and sanitation access gaps.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Características dos domicílios - Resultados do Universo do Censo 2022","publisher":"IBGE","publication_date":"2024-02-23","url":"https://www.ibge.gov.br/en/statistics/social/labor/22836-2022-census-3.html?edicao=39241","claim":"IBGE says the 2022 census data let readers assess household living conditions through water supply, waste disposal, sewage, bathrooms, and piped water, and that the results are disaggregated by color/race and age groups.","locator":"About - Characteristics of Housing Units / Results of the universe","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IBGE is the authoritative census source and the page describes the exact variables and disaggregation available for 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about 2022 census conditions, though published later.","ruler_attribution":"Contextual baseline rather than a ruler-specific policy result.","contrary_evidence":["The page itself is a data-release description, not a welfare evaluation.","It does not isolate Bolsonaro-specific causal effects."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.8","6B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across IBGE, UNICEF, World Bank, Planalto/gov.br, MDS/MEC/MS/Anatel, and a small amount of Reuters-syndicated reporting.

Accepted sources were kept only when they added a distinct claim, not a paraphrase:
- Child poverty, school exclusion, food insecurity, and housing/sanitation from UNICEF, World Bank, and IBGE.
- Direct Bolsonaro-era welfare policy actions on cash transfers, conditionalities, education internet access, vaccination, indigenous health, and housing.
- Administrative correction and targeting evidence for Auxílio Brasil.

Rejected material fell into these buckets:
- Purely promotional or duplicative government pages that repeated the same Auxílio Brasil or Internet Brasil claim without adding a new factual unit.
- General 2023-2025 background pages that did not add a 2022-specific claim.
- Macroeconomic or electoral pieces already handled in 5B/4B and not directly tied to social welfare delivery.
- Out-of-period material unless it was clearly retrospective about 2022 and added a new fact.
- Weak or redundant copies of the same source claim across multiple mirrors.

**Remaining gaps**
- I still do not have a strong independent evaluation of the quality and reach of Bolsonaro-era health and education delivery at the subnational level. The dossier has policy and some outcome evidence, but not a full implementation audit.
- Better independent evidence on racial and regional distribution within 2022 social-service delivery would strengthen 6B.3 and 6B.8.
- The evidence on whether social programs were used as political loyalty tools is suggestive but not definitive; more granular beneficiary-flow or audit evidence would help.
- A direct independent evaluation of 2022 school connectivity and health campaign take-up would improve confidence on 6B.2 and 6B.5.
